1News file - (June 22nd, 2022)
  
               Welcome to MSC Nastran 2022.2
  
   MSC Nastran brings powerful new features and enhancements for engineering
   solutions in several releases through the year. Key enhancements in
   Version 2022.2 are summarized below. Addtional details can be found in
   the MSC Nastran Verison 2022.2 Release Guide.
  
     MSC Nastran 2022.2 Features and Enhancements
  
     ACMS Robustness, Improved Diagnostics and New User Guide
     - Improved ACMS diagnostic messages
     - New "singularity.bdf" output file containing massless mechanism info
     - New SLDSKIN Case Control command to convert skinned-shell elements
       to membrane-only behavior.
     - New ACMS User's Guide
  
     Nonlinear
     - S2SNP (Segment-to-Segment Nodal Penalty) contact technology to support
       permanent glue in SOL 400 and all 100 series solution sequences
     - BOLT1 (1D and 2D) definition for easier bolt modeling
     - Heat Transfer (HSTAT - HTRAN) Chaining analysis
     - SOL 106 & 129 to SOL 400 Translator
  
     Results
     - HDF5 performance improvement to support 32-bit output format and new
       method LZ4 for compression options
  
     Modules
     - Support an external module which can be assembled into a model with
       already existing modules
  
     Composites
     - Cuntze-Bold composite failure and material model
  
     eNVH
     - 1-D Analytic trim (PEM) material model for high-frequency Vibro-acoustics
  
     Real Coupled Modes
     - Acceleration method introduced for large model performance improvement
     - Support added in SOL 200 and SOL 400 (Analysis=LINEAR) solution
       sequences.
  
     Rotodynamics
     - The bent rotor initial deformation, as well as the added constraints,
       can be now requested through the updated ROTBENT case control command
  
     Fatigue
     - Continued expansion of CAEfatigue analysis support including STROUT=4
1     stress scaler response time history and factor of safety analysis
  
     Feature Deprecation
     - The SOL 600 nonlinear solution sequence and RC Network Thermal Solver
       has been deprecated and removed from the software and documentation
  
     Documentation
     - The complete documentation set is provided in a separate installer and
       when installed is available at: MSC_DOC_DIR/doc/pdf_nastran directory,
       where MSC_DOC_DIR is the directory where documentation was installed.
       This help set includes cross references between documents, and links to
       how-to videos, and example files
  
     Individual MSC Nastran documents are available for download from the
       Simcompanion Website at:
       http://simcompanion.hexagon.com/
  
     These documents were updated for the MSC Nastran 2022.2 Release
  
         1.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 Installation and Operations Guide
         2.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 Quick Reference Guide
         3.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 Release Guide
         4.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 Linear Statics Analysis User's Guide
         5.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 Dynamic Analysis User's Guide
         6.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 Superelements User's Guide
         7.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 Rotordynamics User's Guide
         8.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 Demonstration Problems Manual
         9.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 Nastran Embedded Fatigue User's Guide
        10.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 Design Sensitivity and Optimization
        11.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 Nonlinear User's Guide SOL 400
        12.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 DMAP Programmer's Guide
        13.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 High Performance Computing User's Guide
        14.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 New Verification Manual
        15.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 DEMATD Guide
        16.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 Explicit Nonlinear (SOL 700) User's Guide
        17.  MSC Nastran 2022.2 ACMS User's Guide (New)
  
   Please refer to  MSC_DOC_DIR/doc/pdf_nastran/nastran_library.pdf
   for the complete document set:
  
  
     Feature Deprecation List
     To streamline the MSC Nastran program and simplify ongoing maintenance
     activity, some obsolete capabilities have been identified and tagged for
     removal. This activity started in 2021 and continues through 2022.
     Please review the list of features marked for deprecation below to
     ensure that there will be no disruption to your use of MSC Nastran.
     If you see a feature that you currently use and do not wish to lose,
     contact MSC Technical Support to report it.
  
1    Features tagged for removal:
     - TAUCS solver
     - Obsolete DMAP modules
     - SSSALTERS
  
     Refer to the MSC Nastran Release Guide for more details.
  
   Additional information about the release can be found at the MSC Nastran
   Product Support page: http://simcompanion.hexagon.com
  
   The support page provides links to these valuable information:
      * A searchable Knowledge Base containing examples and answers to thousands
        of frequently asked questions written by MSC Software subject-matter
        experts.
      * Peer-to-peer Discussion Forums enabling you to post questions for your
        MSC Software products and receive answers from other users worldwide.
      * A list of known issues with the product and any workarounds.
      * Instructions on how to contact technical support
      * A mechanism for sending us product feedback or enhancement requests.
      * Hardware and software requirements.
      * Examples and Tutorials
      * and much more.
  
   For information on training, please visit our Training web site
  
      https://www.mscsoftware.com/msc-training
  
